 "layer_cap": "M5",
 "structural_change": "STW-S81c-TOK4-BAND 10-22 (STEWARD-S81c item, S81.STA.PAR.3): gunit l1f clock-rule successor. l1f_m hung 25,954 sinks on ONE clk (TT spread 162 / FF 139 ps, trial GRT overflow 595): the front is cut at existing registers into 3 hard row bands (A_lo / F / A_hi, ~7.5k / ~10k / ~7.5k flops), each its own small tree, under a single-root wires-only parent (dsdv_gunit_l1f_bp, < 0.6 mm: plain flop-to-flop hops, ZERO latency change; lockstep vs dsdv_gunit_l1f in the dsdv_gunit golden bench, run_l1f_band_lsw.sh).",
 "why_floorplan": "middle row band: stack inputs on the W face (485 pins / 151 um = 3.2/um, as l1f_m's W face), the 3,584-b SC store + write decode + beat read / forward in the W two thirds, merge (fold -> m1 -> cx8_2) + gather + the 246-b output stage on the E third under the E pins; S face = A_lo seam (sv_lo / control out, sort #0 in), N face = A_hi seam.",
 "job": {
